o death, and one full line to keep…","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Kings 17:21","note":"He stretched himself on the child three times, and cried to Yahweh, and said, “Yahweh my God, please let this child’s soul come into him again.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Job 7:4","note":"When I lie down, I say, ‘When will I arise, and the night be gone?’ I toss and turn until the dawning of the day.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 60:6","note":"God has spoken from his sanctuary: “I will triumph. I will divide Shechem, and measure out the valley of Succoth.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H4059","lemma":"מָדַד","transliteration":"middad","gloss":"to extend"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}